From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Put the display engine behind
 IOMMU1

The mixer keeps a layer's buffer address in one 32-bit register and sets
a 32-bit DMA mask, and the DRM device allocates and imports its buffers
through the mixer device. RAM starts at 0x40000000, so on a board with
more than 3 GiB a buffer can lie above 4 GiB: the DMA API then copies it
through a bounce buffer, and a buffer imported from another driver is
refused unless it is one contiguous range of DMA addresses.

The display engine is master 2 of the second IOMMU (manual chapter 10).
Behind the IOMMU its buffers get 32-bit addresses wherever the pages
are, and scattered pages form one contiguous range. Put the mixer
there, as the H6 does for its mixer. The "display-engine" node gets no
property: the DMA device of the DRM device is the mixer.

Not covered: the other masters of the second IOMMU, the deinterlacer,
G2D and EINK, which have no node.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: the display engine scans out through the
IOMMU, from a page above 4 GiB at a 32-bit address, with the same
picture as without it; a fault on an unmapped address is reported and
the picture recovers once the address is back.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 384e13a004b3..b9e48dbcbdad 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -1299,6 +1299,7 @@ mixer0: mixer@5100000 {
 			clock-names = "bus", "mod";
 			resets = <&de_top RST_DE_TOP_DISP0>;
 			power-domains = <&pck600 PD_DE_SYS>;
+			iommus = <&iommu1 2>;
 			status = "disabled";
 
 			ports {
